WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.476
Levent Alpöge proposed this proof, working with Claude. YiweiIvy built the atlas.

2
00:00:04.476 --> 00:00:10.242
Each star is a Lean declaration. Press / to search all 804,912 in James Shore’s dependency data.

3
00:00:10.242 --> 00:00:15.541
Arrows point to declarations a proof uses. Focus the graph and press E to inspect a reference.

4
00:00:15.541 --> 00:00:21.234
Choose “Trace a proof path” to follow 13 declarations from the Riemann hypothesis to a prime-sum bound.

5
00:00:21.234 --> 00:00:28.846
Press Play. The numbered stops follow direct references, and the inspector changes with each stop.

6
00:00:28.846 --> 00:00:33.931
The source link opens the selected declaration at its exact line in the pinned Lean release.

7
00:00:33.931 --> 00:00:38.739
Corpus groups the same graph by folder or file. Bigger stars contain more declarations.

8
00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:43.493
Inspect a link for the counts of type and body references crossing between two groups.

9
00:00:43.493 --> 00:00:47.980
Return to Network and turn on Evidence. The star colors now show review states.

10
00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:53.562
Move the slider back to the first position. Every star is unreviewed before the first recorded check.

11
00:00:53.562 --> 00:01:00.341
Play the dated checks. The inspector shows the direct finding separately from the state of its dependencies.

12
00:01:00.341 --> 00:01:06.402
Choose Contribute verification on the declaration you checked. Include your method and a source.

13
00:01:06.402 --> 00:01:10.000
Explore the graph at yiweiivy.github.io/riemann-hypothesis-atlas/
